# Orchestrator and WhatsApp

Canonical: `docs/PRODUCT_BEHAVIOR.md`, `docs/specs/TRANSFER_INTENT_GROUNDING_SPEC.md`, `docs/specs/SPEND_CHECK_BEFORE_SEND_SPEC.md`.

- OrchestratorModule has no WhatsApp send. `ActionExecutorService` stays in WhatsappModule.
- Every turn: `propose_turn` then `ActionValidatorService`. Unknown/ineligible/medium → `reply_only`.
- Closed-send utterances (`thanks`, “you already sent it”) must not `show_surface transfer_wizard` or `fill_wizard`. Mid-wizard “I already sent the account” is not closed.
- Vague first sends (`shouldPauseForSpendCheck`) stay `reply_only`. Promote `reply_only` → wizard only when purpose is already stated, or a spend-check is in progress and they proceed, plus actionable sanitized hints.
- Transfer wizard is `TransferDraft`, not `ConversationSession`. After `EXECUTED`, cancel active drafts and record the success fact in chat history.
- Never put PIN/KYC in `WhatsappMessage.textBody` or goldens.
- Validator or surface changes: update `golden-dialogues.json` and run `npm run orchestrator:golden` plus targeted Jest.
